Why modules/ is a boundary and not a merge
------------------------------------------
The three engines were developed as standalone projects and folded in
unmodified. They live under spyglass_pro/modules/ rather than merged into
the package root because runner.py puts that directory on sys.path and the
engines import one another as top-level packages — lens_extender uses
absolute `lens_extender.*` imports throughout. Keeping the vendored tree
separable is what makes a future sync a directory replacement instead of a
three-way merge, and it keeps merge-layer code from drifting into engine
code.

